# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 18 — Acceptance Criteria / Audit Specification

---

# Purpose

This section defines measurable acceptance criteria for DigiSwasthya.

Each criterion is an audit statement:

```
User should be able to...
Expected Result
Pass
Fail
```

If a criterion fails, the product is incorrect relative to this PDD.

This catalogue starts with critical criteria across all domains and is intended to grow into thousands over time.

---

# How to Use

- Every criterion has an ID.
- Criteria map to journeys, entities, state machines, calculations, and permissions.
- Pass requires exact expected business result, including what did not change.
- UI cosmetics alone never satisfy a criterion.

---

# A. Authentication & Access

## AC-A01 Login valid user
- User should be able to log in with valid credentials.
- Expected: Access granted to role home; session active.
- Pass: User enters product. Fail: Valid user blocked without suspension reason.

## AC-A02 Login suspended user
- Suspended user attempts login.
- Expected: Access denied with suspension messaging.
- Pass: No operational access. Fail: Suspended user operates trade.

## AC-A03 Forgot password
- User resets password through approved flow.
- Expected: New password works; old password fails.
- Pass: Only new credential authenticates. Fail: Old still works or reset without verification.

## AC-A04 First login invite
- Invited staff accepts invite and sets credentials.
- Expected: User status Active; belongs to inviting business.
- Pass: Staff can login to correct business. Fail: Orphan user or wrong business link.

## AC-A05 Logout
- Logged-in user logs out.
- Expected: Session ended; protected actions require login.
- Pass: Post-logout action denied. Fail: Session still privileged.

