# I. Returns & Credit Notes

## AC-I01 Raise return on delivered goods
- Pharmacy submits valid return.
- Expected: Return Submitted; stockist notified.
- Pass: In review queue. Fail: Auto-credited immediately.

## AC-I02 Return undelivered blocked
- Return before delivery.
- Expected: Blocked.
- Pass: No return. Fail: Return created.

## AC-I03 Return qty > delivered blocked
- Excess qty.
- Expected: Blocked.
- Pass: No submit. Fail: Accepted excess.

## AC-I04 Approve return
- Stockist approves.
- Expected: Credit eligibility created; no silent invoice rewrite.
- Pass: Approved status. Fail: Invoice lines edited historically.

## AC-I05 Issue credit note
- Stockist issues credit from approved return.
- Expected: Credit Note Issued; remaining = amount; pharmacy notified.
- Pass: Credit available. Fail: Amount wrong or missing.

## AC-I06 Credit > approved return blocked
- Over-credit attempt.
- Expected: Blocked.
- Pass: No over-credit. Fail: Excess credit issued.

## AC-I07 Reject return
- Reject with reason.
- Expected: No credit note from that return.
- Pass: No financial credit. Fail: Credit issued anyway.

## AC-I08 Damaged goods not restocked sellable
- Approved damaged return disposition.
- Expected: Quarantine/destroy, not Available sellable.
- Pass: Not sellable. Fail: Auto Available.

